    }
   ],
   "gap": "The full treatment promised by proved=annex:p15.countably-generated-radon-nikodym is not supplied for the sigma-finite assembly. On each block D_i with nu(D_i)>0 the finite construction yields an F_{D_i}-measurable f_i with mu|_{D_i}(B)=int_B f_i d(lambda_i), lambda_i=nu|_{D_i}/nu(D_i), on the trace space (D_i,F_{D_i}); the proof then sets f=f_i/nu(D_i) on D_i and asserts directly 'Summing its nonnegative integrals over the disjoint blocks yields int_A f dnu = sum_i mu(A cap D_i) = mu(A)' (handbook/annex/p15/density-and-product-exercises.tex 185-193). The per-block identity int_{A cap D_i} f dnu = mu(A cap D_i) is not derived: it needs that, for D in F with 0<nu(D)<infinity and nonnegative F_D-measurable g on D, the integral of g over (D,F_D,nu|_D/nu(D)) equals nu(D)^{-1} times the nu-integral over Omega of the zero extension of g (transfer of integrals from the trace space to Omega, and scaling of the measure). Neither this proof, nor the owned trace section (thm:p15-w02c-p15-003-trace-generation and thm:p15-w02c-p15-003-block-data, which stop at the hypotheses of the finite case and at measurability of the glued density), nor any other route file (handbook/parts/p15/integration-expectation.tex defines int_A only as integration of f 1_A on the same space) proves it; so the representation int_A f dnu = mu(A) on the sigma-finite space and the finite-a.e. transfer from lambda_i-null to nu-null sets lack a written step.",
   "blocker": null
  },
